{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 and Mathlib proofs that no directed strongly regular graph exists for 28 parameter sets (v, k, t, λ, μ). A directed strongly regular graph is a 0-1 matrix A with zero diagonal, all row and column sums equal to k and A² = tI + λA + μ(J − I − A). Nine of the parameter sets are those of the paper below: (50, 11, 7, 0, 3), (68, 13, 7, 0, 3), (100, 16, 7, 0, 3), (108, 19, 9, 0, 4), (55, 16, 12, 1, 6), (66, 10, 5, 4, 1), (91, 12, 6, 5, 1), (96, 15, 10, 9, 1) and (28, 6, 3, 2, 1); the tenth set of the paper, (48, 9, 5, 0, 2), is not formalized. The same lemmas exclude eight further sets, and a formalized complement lemma excludes eleven complementary sets. The proofs compare the rank of A − θI, for a root θ of the quadratic x² − (λ − μ)x − (t − μ), with a submatrix of A prescribed at one vertex. For (28, 6, 3, 2, 1) one case is a SAT refutation whose LRAT certificate the Lean kernel checks with decide +kernel. The theorems use only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound.",
